From: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] config_file: persist the dedicated network MAC value

mac_addr=3 selects a pre-generated, per-network address supplied through
mac_value.  The text parser accepts both fields, but the file backend only
writes mac_addr.  SAVE_CONFIG therefore turns a working private address into
00:00:00:00:00:00 after the next restart.

Write mac_value whenever the dedicated-per-ESS mode is selected.  This keeps
the address stable across restarts while leaving address generation and
rotation policy outside wpa_supplicant, as intended by mac_addr=3.

Signed-off-by: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 wpa_supplicant/config_file.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/config_file.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/config_file.c
@@ -950,2 +950,5 @@
	write_int(f, "mac_addr", ssid->mac_addr, -1);
+	if (ssid->mac_addr == WPAS_MAC_ADDR_STYLE_DEDICATED_PER_ESS)
+		fprintf(f, "\tmac_value=" MACSTR "\n",
+			MAC2STR(ssid->mac_value));
 #ifdef CONFIG_MESH
